 "notes": "Headline curve: 'Yb+/Sr (95% C.L.)' from the top panel of Fig. 6, the limit on the linear scalar-photon (dilaton) coupling d_gamma^(1), identical to the canonical Damour-Donoghue d_e with kappa = sqrt(4 pi G) (Eq. 31). Extracted from the vector paths of fig_6_v2.pdf in the e-print (salmon RGB 0.98/0.50/0.45), axes calibrated on tick-label positions; calibration cross-checked against the paper's analytic relation d^(1)_gamma = 2.0e16 (f/Hz) A_alpha(f) (Eq. 24). The 95% C.L. curve is a jagged frequency spectrum; reported points are its upper envelope in 100 log-mass bins (this envelope coincides with the boundary of the shaded excluded region). Mass range 1.03e-20 to 7e-17 eV corresponds to the stated frequency range 2.5e-6 to 1.7e-2 Hz via m = h f. Standard Halo Model with local density 0.3 GeV/cm^3 assumed; stochastic amplitude degradation factor ~3 included by the authors. The paper also bounds d_me-d_g, d_q-d_g, quadratic couplings, a Higgs portal coupling A, and 1/f_a (axion-gluon, Fig. 10), but presents the d^(1)_gamma Yb+/Sr limit as its main new exclusion (Sec. 5.1 and Conclusion).",
